WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.080
- Speaking of music,

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:04.020
I found out that you're like
a huge Garth Brooks fan.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.010
- I am for real,

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.440
and that actually ties into
our movie a little bit.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.850
- [Kelly] I know, so that's where

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.530
you're doing the dance, isn't it?

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:11.800
It's like different lyrics.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.392
- It is an homage to the dance, yes.

00:00:13.392 --> 00:00:14.271
- [Kelly] Yes, yes.

00:00:14.271 --> 00:00:15.104
- That I sing.

00:00:15.104 --> 00:00:15.937
- I recognize the song, the melody, yeah.

00:00:15.937 --> 00:00:17.708
- Yes yes yes, which you sang
your version of the dance.

00:00:17.708 --> 00:00:19.048
- Brilliantly as it can be.

00:00:19.048 --> 00:00:19.939
- Oh at the Kennedy Center!

00:00:19.939 --> 00:00:21.032
But thank you!

00:00:21.032 --> 00:00:21.931
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:21.931 --> 00:00:22.950
You made Garth Brooks cry.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.020
- [Kelly] Aw, thank you!

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:24.853
- And everybody watching it was truly.

00:00:24.853 --> 00:00:26.010
- I watched that like 30 times.

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.422
- [Luke] Yeah.

00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.400
- [Kelly] Thank you!

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.233
- Literally during the filming we

00:00:29.233 --> 00:00:30.510
we were talking a lot about Garth Brooks

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:33.720
and Billy actually wrote that song

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:34.770
during the filming of it.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.851
It was not something
that was totally planned.

00:00:36.851 --> 00:00:37.684
- Oh, really?

00:00:37.684 --> 00:00:38.517
- [Billy] Yeah.

00:00:38.517 --> 00:00:39.350
- It came out of a
conversation that we had about

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.183
what music we liked.

00:00:40.183 --> 00:00:41.174
- Yeah.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.007
- Yeah, because we didn't know each other

00:00:42.007 --> 00:00:42.840
before we started shooting.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:43.949
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:43.949 --> 00:00:45.300
- And we were trying to
get to know each other.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.470
So I said to him, you know,

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:47.550
what kind of music do you like?

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.290
And he said, "Actually,
I love country music.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:51.450
and my favorite singer is Garth Brooks."

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.090
And I was thinking my character
in the movie at the end

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.380
I don't want to give it all away,

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.200
but you know he needs
to make a grand gesture.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.385
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:59.385 --> 00:01:00.968
- You know, 'cause he's
in love with this guy

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.600
but has a hard time expressing himself.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.539
We both do.

00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:04.372
That's what "Bros" is about.

00:01:04.372 --> 00:01:05.205
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:05.205 --> 00:01:06.038
- And I thought, you know what?

00:01:06.038 --> 00:01:08.550
I like the idea of a gay man singing

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.860
a Garth Brooks inspired country song.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.500
A love song, to the guy he's in love with.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.390
Even though my character
doesn't love country music

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:16.992
but his does.

00:01:16.992 --> 00:01:18.180
So, that's part of the gesture.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.013
- Yeah.

00:01:19.013 --> 00:01:20.220
- You have great taste in real life.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.509
I'm just saying.

00:01:21.509 --> 00:01:22.342
- [Luke] Thank you very much.

00:01:22.342 --> 00:01:23.175
Thank you.

00:01:23.175 --> 00:01:24.008
- I know, I noticed you liked country

00:01:24.008 --> 00:01:24.841
so I gave you George Straight vinyl.

00:01:24.841 --> 00:01:26.872
- Yes, back that was so-

00:01:26.872 --> 00:01:28.069
- Just saying, dip into that.

00:01:28.069 --> 00:01:28.902
- Absolutely, Amarillo by morning.

00:01:28.902 --> 00:01:30.693
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh, it's so good.

00:01:30.693 --> 00:01:32.040
- He's a real country fan.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.660
- I actually tried to play
it on your record player.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.160
Your record player
backstage was not working.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.478
- It was not working?

00:01:36.478 --> 00:01:37.311
- It was not working for me.

00:01:37.311 --> 00:01:40.109
- We like to just give
you the vinyl to look at.

00:01:40.109 --> 00:01:40.942
(background laughing)

00:01:40.942 --> 00:01:41.775
- Oh well I took it out

00:01:41.775 --> 00:01:42.608
because I wanted to get going and-

00:01:42.608 --> 00:01:43.441
- We will now fix that.

00:01:43.441 --> 00:01:45.363
- [Luke] Ah yes, heads will roll.

